## Context

R19 was reworded and merged on 2026-09-03 (`DECISIONS.md`, entry
"R19 is reworded from an agreement between two normalizers into a promise about
what a user sees"; `SPEC.md` R19; merge `5282918`). It now reads: in semantic
and hybrid search, when a document and a query write the same word in different
but equivalent forms, the query MUST still find the document; lexical search is
exempt, because there the user has asked for the string as typed and matching it
literally is the promise.

The reword deleted the requirement's only evidence path and put nothing in its
place, deliberately. The character-folding sweep compares two normalizers'
source and cannot decide a promise about what a query returns, so `SPEC.md`
§5.2.8 keeps it as a gate serving no requirement, and `README.md`'s standing row
for R19 went from `partial` / `measured` to **`none` / `inferred`**, saying in
its own prose that nothing of the new shape has been executed.

So a ratified requirement stands on the sheet with no assertion at all. That is
what this ticket builds: the round trip a user makes, driven through the
interface, against any target, with no access to its source.

**Why this is not ticket 0580's.** `README.md`'s goal-3 roster names ticket 0029
and ticket 0580 for R19, and 0580 is goal 3's acceptance spec — but its
instrument is the convergence harness, which drives ticket 0566's assembled
conductor from an empty data directory, and 0566 is blocked behind 0565, 0554,
0575, 0576 and 0577, with 0565 blocked behind 0028, which experiment X5 gates.
This assertion needs none of that. It indexes a corpus through `install` and
`configure`, asks one question through `query`, and reads the answer. Its real
prerequisite is the corpus, which is ticket 0029's. Putting it behind 0566 would
be filing the sheet's only evidence-free ratified requirement behind a blocker
no lane can reach.

**Why it is blocked on ticket 0029 and not on nothing.** R19's own last
paragraph makes which forms count as equivalent a property of the fixture
corpus, per script class, and `README.md`'s roster address for R19 moved to
ticket 0029 in the reword's own sweep. Without pinned pairs there is no pair to
query with, and inventing pairs here would re-open the narrowing the ruling
priced and accepted. **Ticket 0029 is held by another lane: read it, cite it,
and do not edit it.**

